# The one XXL window scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xxl runs at the next Saturday
# 02:00 slot. Same contract as xl-queue.env: set by the weekly review or the
# operator, cleared by the launcher after the run, so a window runs once and is
# never silently repeated.
#
#   XL_CHUNK   - chunk id, used for the harness log name and the ledger row
#   XL_COMMAND - the command exactly as it would be typed after
#                scripts/testing/run_and_log.sh <chunk>
#
# Empty is the normal state and the Saturday entry then exits in a second.
#
# This tier is 8 h and 754 GiB against fem-em-solver-xxl, one run per trailing
# 7 days. It is for what a 2 h xl window cannot hold -- the human-scale coil,
# or a many-drive sweep before the factorisation is reused. Ceilings are
# enforced by scripts/automation/hooks/bash_guard.py, so a command carrying a
# timeout above 28800 s or more than 16 ranks is refused before it starts.

XL_CHUNK=""
XL_COMMAND=""
